# React Frontend Architecture (Strict)

GaliGuide client is a **React SPA (Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS)** communicating with the Vercel Serverless Express API. Full reference: `docs/ARCHITECTURE_CODING_STANDARDS.md`.

## Layer flow

```text
pages / views -> components -> hooks -> lib/api -> Express API (/api/*)
```

## Non-Negotiable Core Rules

- **Zero-Cost Mapping Engine:** Under NO circumstances may the frontend load Google Maps JavaScript API SDK (`maps.googleapis.com`), Mapbox, or any pay-per-load mapping tile provider.
- **OpenStreetMap + Leaflet:** All maps must be rendered with Leaflet (`leaflet`, `react-leaflet`) using standard OpenStreetMap raster tiles (`https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`).
- **Clustering & Heatmap:** Markers must spiderfy at street level (zoom 18) using `leaflet.markercluster`. Density layers must render via `leaflet.heat`.
- **Navigation Action:** Clicking "Get Directions" MUST trigger an anchor with target `_blank` to the zero-cost universal URL:
  `https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=${lat},${lng}`
  This opens the native Google Maps mobile app on Android/iOS or web browser for free.
- **Phone Action:** Dialing vendor phone numbers MUST use `<a href="tel:${vendor.phone}">` when valid, and gracefully show the masked phone badge when phone consent is not granted.
- **Anti-Slop Visual Identity:** Adhere strictly to the Indore artisanal color palette:
  - Terracotta Primary: `#9d3e1c`
  - Sage Secondary: `#3d6659`
  - Cream Background: `#f5fbf3`
  - Zero generic purple AI gradients, zero excessive glassmorphism, zero floating blobs. High contrast, clean typography, tactile touch targets (>= 48px on mobile).
